# A node may publish its own readings and nothing else. It cannot subscribe at all,
# and it cannot publish under another device's topic — the broker enforces the
# device boundary so ingestion never has to trust the topic string.
#
# Identity still comes from the certificate SAN once mTLS is in place; this ACL is
# the coarse fence, not the identity check.

user esp32-01
topic write psychron/v1/esp32-01/#

# Contract v2 only, and only its own subtree. A phone that could write under v1
# could pass window summaries off as instantaneous readings; one that could
# write under another device's name could impersonate it.
user phone-01
topic write psychron/v2/phone-01/#
# Alerts flow the other way. Read only: a phone that could publish here could
# raise a storm warning nobody's barometer measured, or clear a real one.
topic read psychron/alerts/#

# The ingestion service reads all telemetry, and the only thing it writes is
# the alerts it derives from it.
user ingest
topic read psychron/v1/#
topic read psychron/v2/#
topic write psychron/alerts/#
